50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are A, B, C, and D. I find D, the Microbiome Atlas, most appealing as a lasting catalogue.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A and B require phenotyping and animal care. C is simulation-heavy. I vote for C, Protein Folding Dynamics.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"C relies on spectroscopy, which is currently unreliable. D is a catalogue, but A and B are risky. I prefer D.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,A is limited by glasshouse bookings and field risks. B is expensive due to animal rates. C is free to compute. I'll go with C.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Midori,,A is too risky with the field sites. B is animal-based. D is a catalogue and the repository is now fast. I vote D.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, are you not worried about the spectroscopy failures for candidate C?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,C combines spectroscopy with simulation. The simulation part is safe and free.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Victoria,,But the structural states depend on that spectroscopy. D is much more robust given the repository's new efficiency.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A fair point, Victoria. However, D's field collection might be hampered by the disasters Midori mentioned.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Midori,,The atlas uses several climate zones; it is more diversified than a single-site study.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I still feel D is the most prudent choice for a long-term national investment.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I still believe the staffing for C is the most secure path.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Shizue and Midori. D is the most stable option.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If the field risks for D are manageable, it is a strong contender. But I still lean toward C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Midori,,I believe D offers the best balance of risk and reward.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
